 },
 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Recovery from a dense lisse open",
 "statement": "If $\\mathcal F$ is lisse on a smooth curve $C_0$ and\n$j:U_0\\hookrightarrow C_0$ is dense, then the adjunction map\n\n$$\n\\mathcal F\\xrightarrow{\\sim}j_*j^*\\mathcal F\n$$\n\nis an isomorphism.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-purity-real-sheaves/sk-i-real-boundary/lem-a1-lisse-middle-extension.md",
  "place": "node lem-a1-lisse-middle-extension, order 2645"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-wf-middle-extension"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "The assertion is clear on $U_0$. At a removed point, lissity on\n$C_0$ makes the local inertia action trivial, so the invariant-stalk\nformula of [lem-wf-boundary-stalk-invariants] identifies the\ntarget stalk with the original stalk: $(j_*j^*\\mathcal F)_{\\bar x}= ((j^*\\mathcal F)_{\\bar\\eta})^{I_x}=(\\mathcal F_{\\bar x})^{I_x}= \\mathcal F_{\\bar x}$, the last equality because $I_x$ acts trivially\non the stalk of a lisse sheaf. The map is the naturality of the\nadjunction at every geometric point, hence an isomorphism.",
   "uses": [
    "lem-wf-boundary-stalk-invariants"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
 "proof_deps": [
  "lem-wf-boundary-stalk-invariants"
 ],
